WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
Peace be upon you, and welcome to the second video of Module Two of our fellowship.

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:08.600
In this session, we'll dive right into fascinating details.

3
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:15.360
We're always used to viewing health merely as a doctor's prescription or a pill we take, hoping for the best.

4
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.600
Yet the reality runs much deeper than that.

5
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.660
In this analysis, we will uncover the hidden roots that shape our health without us even noticing.

6
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:27.600
We'll understand how health isn't simply an individual decision; rather, it's a complex web of interconnected circumstances.

7
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.340
Let's get right into it.

8
00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.680
Imagine this scene with me:

9
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.920
Two neighbors living on the exact same street.

10
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.800
Same age, breathing the same air.

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.280
One of them boasts ironclad health, an athlete...

12
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.160
...moving with vibrant energy every single day...

13
00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.660
...as if starring in a vitamin commercial.

14
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.060
The other is quite the opposite:

15
00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:45.980
His health is constantly declining, always sick with the flu and fatigued...

16
00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.320
...a regular customer at local clinics...

17
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:50.720
...the neighborhood pharmacy practically opens up in the morning just for him.

18
00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.400
We see this scene all the time.

19
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.040
And this stark contrast raises a vital question:

20
00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.780
Is this strange disparity simply a matter of genetic luck?

21
00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.980
Meaning one had good fortune while the other drew a losing card?

22
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.380
Or is it about the skill of the doctors?

23
00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:07.240
In truth, reducing it purely to genetics or doctors does injustice to reality.

24
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.340
The story isn't just a surgeon's scalpel or the genetic sequence we were born with.

25
00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:17.800
The story is a hidden force playing the lead role in our health, which in science we term the 'Determinants of Health'.

26
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:23.220
In short, these are the conditions and environments in which we are born, grow, work, and age.

27
00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.680
Not medical decisions inside the examination room.

28
00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.460
We are talking about a complex tapestry of conditions, mostly outside our direct personal control...

29
00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.220
...yet shaping our daily lives.

30
00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:34.120
To understand this fabric, let's deconstruct all its layers.

31
00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:37.160
Layer One: Biology and individual behavior.

32
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.840
It always starts with genetics, age, sex, and family medical history.

33
00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.680
For instance, if diabetes runs in the family, that's a genetic predisposition increasing the odds.

34
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.120
But stay with me: a genetic predisposition is not a definitive death sentence.

35
00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.720
The gene exists dormant, waiting for something to trigger it awake.

36
00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.660
And here is where our habits come into play:

37
00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:57.880
Nutrition, hydration, sleep quality, physical activity, and smoking.

38
00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.760
These behaviors are what modulate genetic risks.

39
00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.480
Yet even these habits do not occur in a vacuum.

40
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:08.580
People don't simply wake up one morning deciding to turn into a green wellness avatar, jogging down the street and sipping smoothies...

41
00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.640
...if their surrounding environment doesn't enable it in the first place.

42
00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:12.400
This brings us to the second layer:

43
00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.440
The environment and socioeconomic status.

44
00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:19.400
Environment and socioeconomic class determine whether healthy habits are accessible or an impossible luxury.

45
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.340
Picture two children:

46
00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.640
One plays in a green park, breathing clean air in a serene rural setting...

47
00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:29.020
...while the other lives on a highway adjacent to two factories, inhaling vehicle exhaust and smog day and night.

48
00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.720
Essentially, that second child eats particulate carbon for breakfast and secondhand smoke for dinner.

49
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.180
His heightened risk of developing asthma isn't bad personal luck...

50
00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.120
...it is an environmental hardship imposed upon him involuntarily.

51
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.360
Add to that noise pollution, water purity, and housing quality.

52
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.360
And overarching all of this: income and education.

53
00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.920
Income and education act like strict building gatekeepers:

54
00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.440
They dictate your ability to live in a clean neighborhood...

55
00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.440
...purchase wholesome, healthy food...

56
00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.680
...and access appropriate medication.

57
00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.800
Those with better educational opportunities cultivate deeper health literacy...

58
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.700
...while economic pressures place suffocating constraints upon families.

59
00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:59.560
To see how these determinants intersect in practice...

60
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.640
...let's hear the story of two diabetic patients.

61
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.220
Both were diagnosed on the very same day with the exact same condition.

62
00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:06.380
The first patient has an excellent income...

63
00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:10.680
...residing in a neighborhood with a premium supermarket selling pristine, fresh produce...

64
00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.540
...and just down the street, an accessible healthcare center where follow-ups are seamless.

65
00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:16.760
He will regulate his blood sugar and manage his condition with total ease.

66
00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.700
The second patient is broke, with severely limited means...

67
00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.560
...living in an isolated area with only corner shops selling cheap biscuits and chips...

68
00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:27.660
...needing two transit transfers and a grueling commute just to reach the nearest clinic for an HbA1c test.

69
00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:31.020
Is the second patient's deterioration caused solely by the disease itself?

70
00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:31.760
Certainly not.

71
00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.480
Socioeconomic and environmental barriers tipped the scales and built an insurmountable wall in front of him.

72
00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.880
Now let's widen the lens further to examine the overarching threat:

73
00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.200
Climate change: the ultimate threat multiplier.

74
00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:47.060
Climate change isn't just rising digits on a weather broadcast and people feeling slightly warm wanting ice cream.

75
00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:51.120
Climate is a hazardous magnifier putting pressure on every determinant of health simultaneously.

76
00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:56.160
It impairs agricultural yields and food security, degrades drinking water quality, and escalates air pollution.

77
00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.700
Meaning right when your home becomes hot and stifling...

78
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.360
...essential basic resources are compromised...

79
00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.200
...and the surrounding environment turns entirely hostile to human health.

80
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.740
That is why advocating for the environment and climate...

81
00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:08.840
...is neither prestige nor a luxury for wool-sweater-wearing activists.

82
00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:13.080
It is a direct defense of our preventive health and the bodies of our families.

83
00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.900
This brings us to the core imperative:

84
00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.840
Empathy first: the mission of the health educator.

85
00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.900
Health education cannot remain perched in an ivory tower detached from reality.

86
00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.640
We frequently hear advice along the lines of:

87
00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.200
'Eat an avocado bowl topped with chia seeds every day...'

88
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.320
'...and eliminate all psychological stress.'

89
00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.400
How delightfully simplistic!

90
00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.700
Scientifically, the advice sounds wonderful and is 100% accurate.

91
00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:33.820
Yet in reality, the price of an avocado alone...

92
00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:36.260
...is enough to induce psychological panic and a 3D stroke for an ordinary citizen!

93
00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:38.340
It is very easy to dispense condescending orders.

94
00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:40.680
However, a smart, compassionate health educator...

95
00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.540
...asks themselves first:

96
00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.160
Is this nutritious food even accessible or affordable in the first place?

97
00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.500
What financial hardships are constricting them...

98
00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.120
...and preventing them from implementing this recommendation?

99
00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.120
Grasping the determinants of health...

100
00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.520
...instills genuine empathy...

101
00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.960
...enabling you to craft grounded messages...

102
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.320
...that genuinely empower people to overcome real-world hurdles.

103
00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:57.380
In conclusion...

104
00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:59.180
...we leave you with this question for reflection:

105
00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.560
What is the most influential hidden factor...

106
00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.020
...governing community health every day?

107
00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:05.440
Is it income, environmental quality, housing infrastructure...

108
00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:07.520
...or accessible healthcare services?

109
00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:09.540
Contemplating the answer to this question...

110
00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.440
...will pave the way for our upcoming video...

111
00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:16.300
...where we translate these facts into practical tools to address climate crises in our Arab region.

112
00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.920
Thank you for watching, and see you in the next video!
